  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 243 PM MDT SUN JUL 26 2026\nSouthwest flow aloft will be the name of the game in the long-\nterm period. With high pressure aloft over the Four Corners \nregion, and troughing over British Columbia, conditions will \nremain warm, dry, and breezy. Later in the week, the high \npressure aloft will begin to shift over the Great Basin, \nallowing for temperatures to rise to around 5 degrees above \nnormal. Afternoon breezes will increase come Saturday and \nSunday, as a shortwave associated with the aforementioned trough\nmoves inland and tightens the pressure gradient over our area. \nA cold front associated with the shortwave will sag south come \nthis weekend, allowing for temperatures to cool to near, or even\nslightly below, normal by Sunday.",
